The files in sources/ are excerpts of United States federal government documents:
three Executive Orders signed by the President (14110, 14148, 14179) and four memoranda
issued by the Director of the Office of Management and Budget, Executive Office of the
President (M-24-10, M-24-18, M-25-21, M-25-22). See sources.json for each file's issuer,
date and permalink.

Each is a "work of the United States Government" and is not subject to copyright in the
United States.

    17 U.S.C. 105(a): "Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work
    of the United States Government, but the United States Government is not precluded from
    receiving and holding copyrights transferred to it by assignment, bequest, or otherwise."
    https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm
    https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105

    17 U.S.C. 101: "A "work of the United States Government" is a work prepared by an officer
    or employee of the United States Government as part of that person's official duties."
    https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec101.htm

The publishing sites say the same:

    whitehouse.gov (source of M-25-21 and M-25-22): "Pursuant to federal law,
    government-produced materials appearing on this site are not copyright protected."
    https://www.whitehouse.gov/copyright/

    bidenwhitehouse.archives.gov (archived White House site, source of M-24-10 and M-24-18):
    "Pursuant to federal law, government-produced materials appearing on this site are not
    copyright protected."
    https://bidenwhitehouse.archives.gov/copyright/

The Executive Orders were taken from the Federal Register (federalregister.gov, published
by the Office of the Federal Register and the Government Publishing Office); the official
PDF for each is linked in sources.json.

Statements checked on 2026-10-09. Outside the United States the status of US government
works can differ.
